# ...but the add-on manifest is source.
!nvda-addon/manifest.ini

# OpenTV: the original Centigram distribution, generated analysis output,
# build products and reference audio.  The distribution and the
# disassembly stay out; the engine's constant tables under data/ are
# deliberately committed instead, so a build needs no Centigram binary.
# See NOTICE for whose work those are.
/TruVoice/
# MindMaker's TextAssist build of TruVoice, kept locally to read voice
# definitions out of.  Another company's product, and not ours to
# redistribute -- what OpenTV takes from it is described in NOTICE.
/TruVoice from text assist/
# The DECtalk source release, kept locally to read its singing model out of.
# Someone else's code under someone else's licence: it is read, never copied,
# and never redistributed from here.  What was read is described in NOTICE and
# in docs/SINGING.md.
/dectalk/
# Open JTalk 1.11, kept locally to read its Japanese front end out of.
# Three-clause BSD (Nagoya Institute of Technology; MeCab by Kudo and NTT; the
# NAIST dictionary by Nara Institute of Science and Technology), so unlike the
# two above it could be redistributed -- it is kept out because it is a
# reference we read, not a part of OpenTV.  See NOTICE for what was read.
#
# The generators read it: lang/jpn/data/jadic.bin is compiled from its dictionary
# and build/Japanese_test/ojt_tables.py from its rule headers, and
# lang/jpn/data/jadic.provenance.txt records the release and the hash of every
# input.  build/check/openjtalk_morph_audit.py compiles its five NJD stages
# into the reference library the parity tool compares against.
/open_jtalk-1.11/
# Phonetics papers the Japanese work is sourced from, kept locally to read.
# Published, copyrighted, and not ours to redistribute: the findings are cited
# in the code and in build/Japanese_test/README.txt, the PDFs stay out.
# open_questions.md is ours and is the point of keeping the folder, so it is
# the one thing in here that is tracked.
/lang/jpn/research/*
!/lang/jpn/research/open_questions.md
/work/
# ...but the Japanese synthesis is SOURCE, not a build product.  It only sits
# under build/ because that is where it was started; it is original work of
# ours, derived from published phonetics rather than from any Centigram
# binary, and nothing else in the project reproduces it.  The generated audio
# is still excluded by the *.wav rule below.
/build/*
!/build/Japanese_test/

# The reference harness is source too, and tools/ja_stage_parity.py imports
# it, so leaving it out would ship a tool that cannot run.  It sits under
# build/check only because that is where the verification binaries go.  The
# library it compiles -- njd-reference.dll -- stays out: it is built from the
# Open JTalk checkout, which is itself not in the repository.
!/build/check/
/build/check/*
!/build/check/openjtalk_morph_audit.py
!/build/check/morphology_followup.py

/ref/
*.wav

# Copies of the Centigram demo texts that sit in the repository root
/ADDRBOOK.TXT
/ADDRESS.TXT
/HOMOGRPH.TXT
/PHONE.TXT
/SAMPLE.TXT

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

